Derived work
------------

SangKey is derived from the 84Key macOS project
(https://github.com/nghialuong/84Key) and preserves its copyright and GPLv3
obligations.

The Vietnamese typing engine is derived from OpenKey
(https://github.com/tuyenvm/OpenKey), Copyright (c) Mai Vũ Tuyên,
licensed under GPLv3. Because the engine is GPLv3, SangKey as a whole is also
distributed under GPLv3. We gratefully acknowledge the OpenKey project for the
core typing logic that makes accurate Vietnamese input possible.

Third-party data
----------------

1. English common-word corpus
   Source: Darius Kazemi Corpora, data/words/common.json
   https://github.com/dariusk/corpora
   Pinned upstream commit: cf30ca27ab176b63623af1ddcfa2447ac07305ba
   Pinned Git blob: 8ec4ea53704dfca63f1ee00852c6bcc15411c49e
   License: Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal.
   Used as the auditable common-word base for automatic English detection.

   The small SangKey-maintained English detector supplement is kept separately
   in core/data/english_supplement.dat and is dedicated to CC0 1.0 by SangKey
   contributors to the extent they hold copyright or related database rights.
   See core/data/ENGLISH_WORDS_PROVENANCE.md for exact provenance.

2. Vietnamese syllable dictionary
   The Vietnamese-by-Telex syllable dictionary is generated from linguistic
   rules by this project. It is not derived from, and does not incorporate, any
   external or scraped word list.

Distribution note
-----------------

SangKey does not embed Sparkle or another in-app updater. The menu update command
opens the project's GitHub Releases page only after an explicit user action.
Release-build tooling such as XcodeGen is not linked into the application and is
covered by its own upstream license.

Public DMGs include LICENSE.txt, NOTICE.txt, THIRD_PARTY_DATA.txt and SOURCE.txt.
SOURCE.txt identifies the exact corresponding-source commit for that binary
distribution. THIRD_PARTY_DATA.txt records the reviewed English detector data
provenance.

All SangKey code changes are distributed under GPLv3 unless a file explicitly
states a different compatible data/content dedication.
